    "difficultyReason": "Find excluded denominator values, including a removable discontinuity, and check the resulting graph.",
    "assessment": {
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "assessedAt": "2026-10-24T03:45:21.700Z",
      "rubricVersion": "mathsmap-cognitive-demand-v1",
      "taskHash": "5e1da13607c2779dafe9981f4b795994b56ca772cd5f6b9d2022916fb62a6d0a",
      "evidence": ".booklet-work/full-imports/s6adv-working-with-functions-11-piecewise-defined-functions-20261024/semantic-packets/assignments/assignment-43de7b56b50acafbdea1/1/generation.json"
    }
  },
  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Determine where the function is discontinuous, using your knowledge of asymptotes and/or natural domains. Check your answer using DESMOS.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$f(x)=\\frac{5}{6-x}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=6$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}6-x&=0\\\\x&=6\\end{aligned}$$\nThe denominator is zero at $x=6$, so the function is discontinuous there. Desmos confirms a vertical asymptote at $x=6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$f(x)=\\frac{3x}{(x-1)(x-3)(x-5)}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,3,5$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}(x-1)(x-3)(x-5)&=0\\\\x&=1,3,5\\end{aligned}$$\nThe function is undefined at these values. Desmos confirms vertical asymptotes at $x=1,3,5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$f(x)=\\frac{x(x+1)}{(x+1)(x+3)}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1,-3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x+3)&=0\\\\x&=-1,-3\\end{aligned}$$\nThe original denominator excludes both values. Cancelling $x+1$ does not restore $x=-1$ to the domain: there is a hole at $(-1,-\\tfrac12)$ and a vertical asymptote at $x=-3$. When checking in Desmos, retain the original domain restrictions; the hole may not be visibly marked.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$f(x)=\\frac{5}{x^2-5x}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0,5$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x^2-5x&=0\\\\x(x-5)&=0\\\\x&=0,5\\end{aligned}$$\nThe function is undefined at these values. Desmos confirms vertical asymptotes at $x=0,5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$f(x)=\\frac{x}{x^2-5x+6}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2,3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x^2-5x+6&=0\\\\(x-2)(x-3)&=0\\\\x&=2,3\\end{aligned}$$\nThe function is undefined at these values. Desmos confirms vertical asymptotes at $x=2,3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q5-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$f(x)=\\frac{x^2-16}{x^2-9}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-3,3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x^2-9&=0\\\\(x-3)(x+3)&=0\\\\x&=-3,3\\end{aligned}$$\nThe numerator is nonzero at both values. Desmos confirms vertical asymptotes at $x=-3,3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
